rmation from a text string. Here’s a simple example:\n```python\ntext = "I visited Paris and Berlin last summer."\nplaces = GeoText(text)\n\n# Get the extracted places\nprint(places.cities)\n```\n\n### Step 3: Analyze Results\nThe `GeoText` object will contain various attributes such as `cities`, `countries`, and `regions`, which you can use to analyze the geographical data extracted from your text.\n\n## Conclusion\n`GeoText` is a powerful tool for anyone needing to extract and analyze geographical information from unstructured text. With simple installation and easy-to-use functions, you can quickly integrate it into your projects.', 'encoding': 'utf-8', 'mode': 'overwrite'}, 'stage': 'before'} 
