raphical entities.\\n3. **Data Utility**: Provides tools to utilize the extracted geographical data effectively.\\n\\n## Installation Instructions\\n\\n### Prerequisites\\nBefore installing `GeoText`, ensure you have Python installed on your machine. You can download it from [python.org](https://www.python.org/downloads/).\\n\\n### Setting Up the Environment\\n1. Open your terminal or command prompt.\\n2. Navigate to the directory where you want to install `GeoText`.\\n3. Run the following command to set up a virtual environment:\\n   ```bash\\n   python -m venv geotext_env\\n   ```\\n4. Activate the virtual environment:\\n   - On Windows:\\n     ```bash\\n     .\\\\geotext_env\\\\Scripts\\\\activate\\n     ```\\n   - On MacOS/Linux:\\n     ```bash\\n     source geotext_env/bin/activate\\n     ```\\n\\n### Installing Dependencies\\nTo install the necessary Python packages, run:\\n```bash\\npip install geotext\\n```\\n\\n## How to Use GeoText\\n1. Import the `GeoText` module in your Python script:\\n   ```python\\n   from geotext import GeoText\\n   ```\\n2. Create an instance of `GeoText` with your text input:\\n   ```python\\n   text = \\"Your text with geographical information here\\"\\n   geo = GeoText(text)\\n   ```\\n3. Access the geographical data:\\n   ```python\\n   cities = geo.cities  # List of cities found\\n   countries = geo.countries  # List of countries found\\n   ```\\n4. Use the extracted data as needed in your application.\\n\\n## Conclusion\\nWith `GeoText`, you can easily extract and utilize geographical information from unstructured text, making it a valuable tool for anyone dealing with location-based data. \\n","encoding":"utf-8","mode":"overwrite"}'}}]}, {'role': 'tool', 'content': '{\n  "path": "geotext/manual.md",\n  "absolute_path": "C:\\\\Users\\\\lucag\\\\SwarmDev_Parallel\\\\ChatDev\\\\WareHouse\\\\geotext_20260531154257\\\\code_workspace\\\\geotext\\\\manual.md",\n  "size": 2008\n}', 'tool_call_id': 'call_kAk84SjiUR7wrMa8bmLBo1Wr', 'me